---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../site";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  section="about"
  description="Kyle James Walker builds browser tools, Rust binaries and Python libraries, and gives them away."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="display text-3xl sm:text-4xl">About</h1>

    <div class="prose-kjw mt-6">
      <p>
        I am Kyle James Walker. I work as a data engineer, and outside that I
        build small tools: things that cut, fold, print or present.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most of them exist because I wanted one and could not find it. The
        laser cutter projects came from wanting boxes that fit the thing going
        in them. The presenting tools came from turning up to talks where the
        setup did not work. The Python libraries came from doing the same
        awkward thing twice at work.
      </p>

      <h2>How the things here work</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/apps/">apps</a> run entirely in your browser. There is no
        account, no upload and no server doing the work. Close the tab and
        nothing of yours is left anywhere but your own machine.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a href="/projects/">projects</a> are on GitHub under an open source
        license. Take them, fork them, ship them in something you sell. No
        attribution needed, though it is nice to hear when something was
        useful.
      </p>

      <h2>This site</h2>
      <p>
        Built with Astro and Tailwind, deployed to GitHub Pages. Every app in
        it is a self-contained project: copy its directory out of the
        repository, run <code>npm install &amp;&amp; npm run dev</code>, and it
        works with nothing of this site attached. That is enforced in CI, not
        just intended.
      </p>
      <p>
        The photograph in the header is a stack of sugar cubes, lit from three
        sides. I took it in 2015.
      </p>

      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href={site.links.github} rel="me noopener">GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href={site.links.linkedin} rel="me noopener">LinkedIn</a></li>
        <li><a href={site.links.email}>Email</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
